<!--Post: 9246--><!--Time: 1109445230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9246"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just saw that story myself.  God Bless her. Apparently she gave the blood sample for the DNA match - which I&#39;m assuming she gave earlier - so yesterday&#39;s DNA testing was a no brainer. They knew they had their man.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
