<!--Post: 9264--><!--Time: 1109454146-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9264"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 1:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->she is a hero, truly courageous<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9264-->
<!--Post: 9293--><!--Time: 1109463914-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9293"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 4:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank God, for her<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9293-->
<!--Post: 9304--><!--Time: 1109466480-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9304"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 5:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was hoping the suspect didn&#39;t have any children but now it&#39;s fortunate he did, at least in the sense that it lead to his capture. How horrible for his son and daughter to have to live through this from now on. I sincerly hope they can. <BR>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9304-->
<!--Post: 9313--><!--Time: 1109468899-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9313"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 5:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think people will be very supportive of the kids.  I agree completely that the daughter was heroic in turning him in.  It would be such a painful thing, but my guess is that she would never have chosen otherwise.  I wonder if he put the kids in Sunday school as part of his religious affiliation.  It would be ironic justice if hiding out in church was in the end his downfall.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9313-->
<!--Post: 9366--><!--Time: 1109484850-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9366"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 10:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;she is a hero, truly courageous&#34; <BR> <BR>Amen to that. Obviously the lack of conscience was not passed on to her.  <BR> <BR>I have to wonder if he was an abuser at home, if that took up some of the need to kill, and if this may have influenced his daughter&#39;s decision. Of course, her site showed a young woman with strong Christian beliefs, so she may have simply known enough to feel morally obligated to turn him in.  <BR> <BR>Ask yourself; say it&#39;s your Dad...could <b>you</b> do it?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9366-->
<!--Post: 9402--><!--Time: 1109494065-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9402"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 12:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I heard on CNN that she didn&#39;t turn him in, she was approached by LE to give a dna sample because they were wondering about a family member. I guess all this will come around sooner or later.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9402-->
<!--Post: 9408--><!--Time: 1109500365-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9408"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Right now I doubt if she cares about anything except her life disintigrating. I&#39;m really glad that she is in Manhattan and not Lawrence. K state is more aggie and teachers college if I remember correctly. Much more of a nurturing environment than KU. KU is not bad, its just full of very competitive people who are self focused and can be rude and hurtful when they smell an open wound. <BR> <BR>Before all you people at KU or from Larryville write me a load of hate mail...I lived there for 6 years and ran into them all the time. So if you haven&#39;t run into them you need to get out more. <BR> <BR>If you feel that you HAVE to slam me, at least be considerate and start a new string. I promise to read it and cry.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9408-->
<!--Post: 9409--><!--Time: 1109501705-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9409"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I visited her website last night and thought about her all day. Then I find out she assisted in the apprehension of her father! Whether the swab was volunteered or not, she had to have known where LE was headed. <BR> <BR>She appears to be a very bright, well rounded young woman. I get an enormous sense of someone who is deeply spiritual, fun loving and engrossed in learning. She shows a genuine concern for others and &#40;like us&#41; spends too much time on the computer. <BR> <BR>“I am a member of a Lutheran Church, but if you talk to me, I&#39;ll tell ya denomination ain&#39;t important, just a personal relationship with God, learning who Jesus is and working on growing in your faith, these sites can help with that…” <BR> <BR>Her core values jump right off the page -- values that are traditionally instilled and nurtured at home. <BR> <BR>Dennis Rader may be a greater mystery in the flesh than he was in the shadows. <BR> <BR>I not surprised to learn he was a grass-measuring, dog-euthanizing martinet of the highest order – but the father of such a thoughtful well rounded child?!! Just where did he go right? <BR> <BR>A monster led the prayers at the Rader family table. No matter how much of a role he played in bestowing values in his kids, it was ultimately an ongoing act of camouflage. The magnitude of his betrayal is unfathomable.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9409-->
<!--Post: 9414--><!--Time: 1109503449-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9414"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Yomama<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Yomama<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 3:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->she is my hero!!! may God richly bless her !!!  i about fell out of my chair when i heard this on the news.  if she didn&#39;t realize that her father may be the killer then she would have no reason to go to law inforcement.  if le had suspicions and went to her then it is wonderful that she willingly cooperated. she is my kind of person !! i cannot give her enough praise .  just imagine how hard that would be to do but thank God she did it. she has alot of back bone.  there are alot of people that are very beholding to her.   see people, miracles do still happen!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9414-->
<!--Post: 9427--><!--Time: 1109521493-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9427"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 8:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yomama: you are right. God raised up a young modern day Queen Esther, who put everything on the line to do what was right. Did she find his murder kit? Or mementos? I&#39;m sure we will learn as time goes by, and I am sure for his family, time is passing very slowly and in an unreal slow-motion. Her family should be proud of her, and her father should be as well. She is a young woman after God&#39;s own heart. <BR> <BR>She is also an example that one chooses their own path by deliberate free will, and no one can blame parents, circumstances gone wrong, bad childhood, hormones, or anything else for their behaviors. In everyone&#39;s heart of hearts, they know right from wrong, and good from bad. I am very proud of her. She is an example to all to stand their ground, no matter what the cost. And many have paid a very high price already for the actions of one man.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9427-->
<!--Post: 9433--><!--Time: 1109522635-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9433"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 8:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I also posted about this wonderful and brave young girl on the talking to Tom thread. We must have been typing at the same time,because I looked before I posted it.I didn&#39;t have time to read all of them but I did look for times, dates, and topics. I like your post very much it tells it like it is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9433-->
<!--Post: 9434--><!--Time: 1109523668-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9434"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 9:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kerri Rader reported to LE two weeks ago that she felt her father could be btk.She gave her dna to be tested for a close btk match.The police did put enough information about the btk to the media,for this to happen,in spite of what a lot of people thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9434-->
<!--Post: 9446--><!--Time: 1109529169-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9446"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neverstop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neverstop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 10:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Like I said two weeks ago, somebody knew. as in the way Unabomber&#39;s brother knew. And lo and behold this time it was a courageous daughter. Let&#39;s be as supportive and helpful as we possibly can. Good girl.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9446-->
<!--Post: 9555--><!--Time: 1109552841-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9555"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Yomama<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Yomama<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 5:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->omg...!!!i didn&#39;t know if she went to them or if they came to her...but if she went to le then wow, what a brave woman!!! i posted somewhere on this board that the darkness just makes the light shine brighter and look at this...!!! oh i&#39;d love to hear her story but i guess it would be hard for her to tell it...there is not enough praise for this woman she is increadable!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9555-->
<!--Post: 9575--><!--Time: 1109558372-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9575"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 6:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Channel 3 is stating that the daughter DID NOT turn him in, she was approached by LE and provided a DNA sample.  Will provide link when it is up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9575-->
<!--Post: 9615--><!--Time: 1109568158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9615"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 9:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Though I know you&#39;re not trying to imply that she should not be praised, I would like to specify that my earlier comment applies regardless of the extent to which she aided LE. I didn&#39;t assume she went out of her way to bring her father to the attention of WPD, but even if she just submitted to a swab after they compelled her to do so, she&#39;s still a hero to me. Tough kid.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9615-->
<!--Post: 9647--><!--Time: 1109577773-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9647"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 12:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The local media have a vested interest in making the local police look as good as possible.In spite of the suprficial &#34;rally of a job well done&#34; that the department and media are presently pushing hard to make take root, anyone who has been following the case must still wonder why Rader, who obviously fits the profile and has rubbed a lot of people the wrong way, was difficult to find at all. <BR> <BR>As a member of the Zoning Board, and Manager of the Compliance Board of Park City, plus being President of his church congregations Rader was was weilding some serious mid-level political and financial clout in a city directly adjacent to Wichita. This guy was not operating under the radar by any stretch of the imagination. <BR> <BR>If the Wichita Police would just break precedence and state: &#34;We regret that it took us so long to solve the case, I personally wouldn&#39;t mind if they added &#34;...but, DAMN ain&#39;t we good&#34;.  <BR> <BR>But as usual they are using political methods to give the appearance that they made no mistakes and 30 years is &#39;just how long it takes to solve a case&#39;, even if it minimizes Rader&#39;s daughter&#39;s monumental, act of selflessness. <BR> <BR>At the press conference one speaker said that &#34;all of the details of the BTK case may never be released&#34;. That statement alone is all telling. I can think no reason do deny even historians all of the facts of the case other than impropriety.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9647-->
<!--Post: 9649--><!--Time: 1109578808-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9649"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 12:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The story I heard is that Dennis Rader has been under surveilane for two weeks prior to his arrest. Sometime during that time the police asked his daughter to provide a DNA to eliminate her father as a suspect. Perhaps she thought by doing this it would eliminate her father from any suspicion. Maybe they told her her father would not volunteer to a routine swab and if she could give one they could use it to routinely eliminate her father as a possible BTK. I don&#39;t know how they could have done this without her telling her father what she did. He was under survielance anyway so he wasn&#39;t going to go anywhere because they would have stopped him from fleeing wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9649-->
<!--Post: 9662--><!--Time: 1109583132-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9662"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 1:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK, folks, please don&#39;t post any links to the personal homepages of Rader&#39;s family.  It&#39;s one thing if they&#39;re mentioned in news stories, but leave their personal stuff out of this.  They&#39;re having a hard enough time dealing with the fact that their father/husband is one of the most notorious serial killers in the last 50 years, and so please respect their privacy at this time and refrain from posting links to anything other than news stories &#40;we&#39;ve been enforcing this in the chatroom also&#41;.  E-mail them to each other if you must, just keep it off the board for the time being. <BR> <BR>And yes, Lostdog, I edited the links out of your posts.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9662-->
<!--Post: 9667--><!--Time: 1109586615-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9667"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 2:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Ed. <BR> <BR>With so much information being unveiled and after trying to do so much with so little, I lost perspective. <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9667-->
<!--Post: 11690--><!--Time: 1111031301-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11690"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 7:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dennis Rader&#39;s Daughter didn&#39;t turn him in and the police did a very good job in help catching this creep, also police caught Rader by tracing the floppy disk back to his church and obtaining a list of people who had computer access. <BR>Thankyou <BR>Megabyte<!--/Text--></td></tr>
